    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156726714": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "University of Auckland Executive Assistant | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Executive Assistant Part-time Campus: Grafton Campus Position Number: 55562847 UoA Department Name: Liggins Institute Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have eight academic faculties and 11 service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and health researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description The opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are looking for a skilled Executive Assistant to join our team. The role will be supporting one or more high profile researchers. The main responsibilities for this role will be diary management and managing email inbox, coordinating local events, fast and accurate minute taking, formatting of presentations and documents, e-card reconciliations, complex travel arrangements. You will enjoy ownership of the work that you do and be empowered to develop your own systems of efficiency and process improvements and contribute ideas to the continuous improvement of our Institute and the wider University. This position is available at 26.25 hours per week until June 2027 , after which it will continue as a permanent /18.75h per week. Subject to the continuation of external research funding, there may be the opportunity for the role to remain at higher FTE/hours beyond this date. The salary range for this position is $63,600 - $79,300 (pro rata) dependent on skills and experience For more detailed information, please refer to the position description . About the team | Mō tō mātou rōpū Our team are a close-knit, high performing bunch, driven by a shared vision to understand how early life events impact lifelong health and contribute to research that is truly life-changing for future generations. About you | He kōrero mōu You will ideally come to us with prior experience in a similar role. A health science background would be an advantage, but not essential. You will have excellent communication and organisational skills, enjoy problem-solving and be methodical in your approach to your work to ensure our academic staff are well supported. You will be a confident EA with a natural ability to engage with a diverse range of people. If you are the kind of person who gets satisfaction from being involved with a wide range of different tasks and people and enjoys thinking one step ahead of others to make sure they have what they need and things get done, you will find this role really rewarding. Important Skills | Nga Pūkenga Motuhake EA/PA experience, preferably supporting senior management level roles Excellent time management, prioritisation and organisation Exceptional professional written and spoken communication Resourceful and skilled at finding new information, acquiring new skills and getting answers Skilled at negotiation and politely guiding others to ensure all stakeholders are well supported and get what they need in a way that is sustainable of your time Intermediate to advanced Microsoft Office skills A problem solver, collaborator and someone who enjoys developing efficiencies and improvements Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online, by the closing date of December 4th to be considered. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting how you can meet the skills and experiences detailed above. If you have any role related questions, please reach out to Lynda Pitcaithly, via l.pitcaithly @auckland.ac.nz , for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. #LI-DNI Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156704949": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Marketing Content Creator",
      "description": "University of Auckland Marketing Content Creator | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Marketing Content Creator Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019759 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties, two large-scale research institutes and a number of professional service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are looking for a creative, audience-focused and detail-oriented Marketing Content Creator to develop compelling content that supports the University of Auckland’s marketing, student recruitment and brand objectives. This role will be responsible for creating high-quality marketing content across digital and print channels, including websites, social media, campaign copy, brochures, flyers, EDMs and promotional materials The Marketing Content Creator reports to the Marketing Manager within the Marketing and Recruitment function of the Strategic Engagement portfolio. Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Marketing and Recruitment is a core enabling function within the Strategic Engagement portfolio, providing specialist marketing and recruitment services across brand, market segmentation, campaigns, events, market research, partnerships, promotional activity and student recruitment. The team is responsible for strengthening the University of Auckland’s brand and reputation and supporting the recruitment of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral students across local and international markets. You will also collaborate with creative suppliers, including designers, photographers, videographers and printers, as required. We have 3 full-time, permanent opportunities available. The full salary range for these roles are $73,400 - $99,400 per annum (Band F). For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the position description . He kōrero mōu | About you The ideal candidate will be a strong writer and creative thinker who understands how to turn information, ideas and campaign objectives into content that connects with audiences and delivers results. You will have excellent copywriting, editing and proofreading skills, with the ability to adapt your writing style from technical and informative to emotional and persuasive. This role will suit someone who is proactive, collaborative and adaptable, with the ability to work autonomously while contributing positively to a busy and creative team environment. Ngā Pūkenga Motuhake | Important Skills Creating compelling, audience-focused marketing content across web, social media, campaign copy, email and print Writing, editing and proofreading content to ensure it is accurate, engaging, accessible and fit for purpose Developing content that supports marketing plans, campaigns and key University initiatives Adapting messaging for different audiences, channels and stages of the customer journey Working with Marketing Managers, Marketing Advisers and Marketing Coordinators to translate briefs and campaign objectives into effective content. Āu ka kawe mai ai | What you will bring You will have a relevant tertiary qualification in marketing, communications, media, design, journalism or a related discipline, or equivalent professional experience. You will also bring: Demonstrated experience producing marketing content across digital and print channels, with strong writing, editing and proofreading skills The ability to tailor content for different audiences, channels and objectives while maintaining a consistent brand voice An understanding of brand, accessibility and inclusive communication principles A strong quality-assurance mindset and exceptional attention to detail Experience working within a large public sector or tertiary organisation would be advantageous. Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of 4th of November 2026 . Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting your interest in the role, your capabilities and relevant experience. Please reach out to Susi Burke, Communications and Marketing Manager - susi.burke@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Marketing Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Coordinator Auckland, New Zealand Brand Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Marketing Content Creator Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156704899": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Marketing Adviser",
      "description": "University of Auckland Marketing Adviser | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Marketing Adviser Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019752 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties, two large-scale research institutes and a number of professional service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description Te whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We're looking for a collaborative, organised and proactive Marketing Adviser to support the delivery of integrated marketing campaigns and promotional activity that strengthens the University of Auckland's brand, supports student recruitment and engages priority audiences. This role offers the opportunity to work across a diverse range of University priorities, which may include undergraduate and postgraduate recruitment, research and innovation, and campus experience services such as accommodation, sport and recreation, library, careers, early childhood education, and student health and wellbeing. Key areas of focus include: Supporting the planning and delivery of integrated marketing campaigns, promotional activity and events across print, digital and social media Coordinating campaign implementation, creative development and content production with internal stakeholders and external suppliers Providing marketing input and advice to support portfolio priorities, campaigns, new programme development and service initiatives Managing multiple timelines, deliverables and competing priorities while maintaining a strong focus on accuracy and customer service Contributing to continuous improvement and effective ways of working across the Marketing and Recruitment function Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Marketing and Recruitment is a core enabling function within the Strategic Engagement portfolio, bringing together specialist expertise across brand, marketing, student recruitment, market research, campaigns, events, partnerships and promotional activity. The team is responsible for strengthening the University of Auckland's brand and reputation and supporting the recruitment of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral students across local and international markets. You'll work collaboratively with colleagues across Marketing and Recruitment, as well as faculties, research institutes, service divisions and specialist teams. This is an opportunity to contribute to a collaborative team environment while gaining exposure to a broad range of marketing activity within one of New Zealand's largest and most complex organisations. This is a full-time, permanent opportunity. The full salary range for this role is $73,400 - $99,400 per annum (Band F) For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the position description . He kōrero mōu | About you We're looking for someone who combines practical marketing experience with strong organisational skills, attention to detail and a collaborative approach. We're particularly interested in people who bring: Experience delivering marketing, campaigns, content, events or promotional activity across multiple channels, including digital and social media Strong organisational and communication skills, with the ability to coordinate multiple priorities, stakeholders and deadlines Confidence working with internal stakeholders and external suppliers to deliver high-quality marketing activity The ability to work both independently and collaboratively, adapting to changing requirements and priorities A proactive, solutions-focused mindset and a commitment to continuous improvement Ngā Pūkenga Motuhake | What you will bring You'll bring the ability to turn marketing plans and ideas into well-coordinated activity that delivers a positive experience for audiences. You will be comfortable working across multiple projects and channels, coordinating creative and content development, and ensuring activity is delivered on time and to the required standards. You'll also bring the confidence to provide practical marketing advice and build positive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of 4th of November 2026. Please include your cover letter and CV, highlighting your skills, experience and interest in the role. As part of your application, please also provide an example of marketing or communications activity you have recently contributed to or delivered. This could include a campaign, promotional activity, event, social media campaign, digital activity, marketing collateral or other relevant work. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. Please reach out to Samantha Edge, Communications & Marketing Manager - samantha.edge@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. #LI -DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Student Support Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Doctoral Candidate Advisor Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Marketing Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156704056": {
      "title": "Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Auckland Marketing Coordinator  | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Marketing Coordinator Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019771 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties, two large-scale research institutes and a number of professional service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description Te whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We're looking for a highly organised, proactive and detail-focused Marketing Coordinator to support the smooth delivery of marketing campaigns, content, events and promotional activity across an assigned portfolio. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to a diverse range of University priorities, which may include undergraduate and postgraduate recruitment, research and innovation, and campus experience services such as accommodation, sport and recreation, library, careers, early childhood education, and student health and wellbeing. Key areas of focus include: Coordinating marketing workflows, campaigns and portfolio initiatives, maintaining schedules, actions, dependencies, approvals and deliverables Supporting Marketing Managers and Advisers with stakeholder coordination, meetings, documentation, follow-up actions and communication of progress Maintaining accurate records, templates, project information and workflow documentation Managing multiple priorities and deadlines while maintaining a strong focus on accuracy and quality Identifying opportunities to improve marketing processes, templates, workflows and ways of working. Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Marketing and Recruitment is a core enabling function within the Strategic Engagement portfolio, bringing together specialist expertise across brand, marketing, student recruitment, market research, campaigns, events, partnerships and promotional activity. This is an opportunity to play a key role in creating structure, consistency and momentum across a busy marketing environment, supporting specialist teams to deliver high-quality activity for diverse audiences. We have two, full-time permanent opportunities available. The full salary range for these roles are $63,600 - $86,100 per annum (Band E) For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the position description . He kōrero mōu | About you We're looking for someone who is highly organised, reliable and solutions-focused, with a strong ability to keep multiple tasks, timelines and stakeholders moving forward. We're particularly interested in people who bring: Demonstrated experience in an administrative, coordination or marketing support role, with the ability to manage schedules, tasks and competing priorities. A proactive, adaptable and collaborative approach, with the ability to work independently while maintaining strong relationships The ability to respond professionally and constructively to changing priorities, requests and challenges A practical, solutions-focused mindset and an interest in improving processes and ways of working You'll have a relevant qualification in marketing, communications, business administration or a related discipline, or equivalent professional experience. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What you will bring You'll bring the ability to create structure, maintain momentum and make sure the details behind marketing activity are well coordinated. You'll also bring a strong customer-service mindset and the confidence to identify potential risks, follow up actions and escalate issues when required, while remaining calm and constructive in a busy environment. Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of 4th of November 2026 . Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting your interest in the role, your capabilities and relevant experience. Please reach out to Susi Burke, Communications and Marketing Manager - [email protected] for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156679721": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Kaiako",
      "description": "University of Auckland Kaiako - Early Childhood Educator - Fixed Term  | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Kaiako - Early Childhood Educator - Fixed Term Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60022983 UoA Department Name: Early Childhood Centres Job Description Join Our Supportive Team of Passionate Early Childhood Educators! Are you a New Zealand-trained and certified Kaiako looking for an inspiring and supportive workplace? At Te Ako o te Tui Early Learning Service , located in the heart of the University of Auckland’s Grafton Campus, we offer a vibrant, purpose-built learning environment designed to support the learning, development and wellbeing of tamariki. As one of the University’s larger early learning services, Te Ako o te Tui offers spacious, thoughtfully designed indoor and new outdoor learning environments that encourage curiosity, independence and meaningful learning experiences. Our experienced and dedicated kaiako work collaboratively to create a strong sense of belonging, where every child is valued, supported and encouraged to thrive. Our exceptional teacher-child ratios allow kaiako to develop meaningful relationships with tamariki and whānau, engage in intentional teaching and respond thoughtfully to each child's individual learning journey. Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking a passionate and committed fixed term , ECE qualified and Certificated Kaiako to join our team at Te Ako o te Tui. Our service is a purpose-built, well-established early childhood centre licensed for 90 tamariki aged from 3 months to 6 years. This role is primarily based in our under-2s room, supporting up to 30 tamariki with a 1:3 ratio. There is also the opportunity to work across the full age range as required, providing flexibility to support the needs of our diverse community. This is a fixed term (12 months), full-time position (40 hours per week) with a rotational shift that changes fortnightly. The salary range for this role is above full pay parity Step 1: $60,701 to Step 11: $101,719 (see our pay structure HERE ). A full description of the role is available in the position description HERE He kōrero mōu | About you You are an enthusiastic and reflective kaiako who brings both heart and intention to your teaching practice. You are passionate about creating meaningful learning experiences and understand the importance of relationships, responsiveness, and intentional teaching. You are confident working within a team, open to professional growth, and committed to ongoing learning. You value diversity and inclusion, and you strive to create an environment where all kaiako, tamariki and whānau feel a strong sense of belonging. You bring a sound understanding of pedagogical practice, including Te Whāriki , and are competent in planning, assessment, and compliance requirements. You may already have some foundation in te reo Māori, or you are motivated to grow this as part of your teaching journey. Most importantly, you are someone who takes pride in your practice, contributes positively to team culture, and is committed to making a meaningful difference in the lives of tamariki. E rapua ana mātou | We are seeking We are seeking a passionate, reflective, and intentional kaiako who is committed to providing high-quality learning experiences and contributing meaningfully to a collaborative team culture. You will: Be a New Zealand qualified and certificated teacher who demonstrates genuine care, respect, and advocacy for tamariki Bring experience working across all age groups, with strong confidence in supporting tamariki within a mixed-age environment, fostering holistic learning and development in a culturally diverse setting Demonstrate strong pedagogical knowledge, with the ability to design and implement intentional teaching strategies, and make learning visible through meaningful assessment and planning Show a clear understanding of Te Whāriki and how it informs curriculum design and responsive teaching practice Actively uphold and reflect Te Tiriti o Waitangi in your practice, with a willingness to grow your understanding of tikanga and te reo Māori Build and sustain respectful, trusting relationships with tamariki, whānau, and colleagues, recognising the importance of whakawhanaungatanga Work collaboratively within a team, contributing to shared thinking, internal evaluation, and continuous improvement Be organised and proactive in managing planning, assessment, and compliance responsibilities Demonstrate a growth mindset, engaging in reflective practice, professional learning, and ongoing development. Contribute positively to team culture, upholding professionalism and high standards of practice. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university, guided by a commitment to excellence and service to our communities. With more than 6,000 academic and professional staff, we support a diverse community of over 47,000 students. Guided by our values , we work collaboratively to advance knowledge, foster equity and inclusion, and contribute meaningfully to New Zealand’s social, cultural, and economic well-being. We cultivate an environment that supports your growth and rewards excellence with a range of staff benefits , including: Above Full Pay Parity (see our pay structure HERE ) and five weeks of annual leave Discounted public Transport for permanent and long-term fixed term staff Discounted parking and childcare Superannuation/KiwiSaver , matching up to 6.75% Leading, and inclusive parental leave provisions Career development opportunities and a range of benefits, including discounted insurance , memberships , and on‑site amenities Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by Thursday, 5 November 2026 . Your application should include: A brief cover letter outlining your interest in the role and how your skills align Your updated CV Please note that we do not accept email applications. For a confidential discussion, you are welcome to contact Indira Boppana, Centre Leader via i.boppana@auckland.ac.nz #LI-DNI Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Kaiako - Early Childhood Educator Auckland, New Zealand Kaiako - Early Childhood Educator Auckland, New Zealand Property Manager - Commercial & Retail Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Kaiako - Early Childhood Educator - Fixed Term Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156672990": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Pathways Programmes Teacher Placement",
      "description": "University of Auckland Pathways Programmes Teacher Placement - Expression of Interest  | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Pathways Programmes Teacher Placement - Expression of Interest Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60011999 UoA Department Name: Schools and Community Engagement Company Description Schools and Community Engagement | Strategic Engagement University of Auckland | Waipapa Taumata Rau At the University of Auckland, we are committed to creating transformative educational opportunities that empower young people to succeed. Through our Pathway Programmes, we work alongside schools, communities, whānau and educators to strengthen educational outcomes and support students on their journey to tertiary study. We're looking for an experienced educator and relationship builder to join our Schools and Community Engagement team as a Pathway Programmes Teacher Placement . Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity This is a unique opportunity for a current or former educator to contribute to programmes that are making a measurable difference for Māori and Pacific learners and helping shape the future of education across Tāmaki Makaurau. Working closely with the Pathway Programmes Manager, you will support the delivery, development and growth of several high-impact initiatives, including: UE Success - partnering with 19 Auckland secondary schools to achieve University Entrance parity for Māori and Pacific learners by 2030. The Pacific Academy – A tutoring programme offered throughout terms 2 and 3 supporting 1,000+ Māori and Pacific students with NCEA maths and science externals. STEM Online NZ – An online teaching and learning platform to support students and teachers with maths and science external preparation, with over 19,000 students registered nationally. Auckland Mathematics Challenge - is a series of fast-paced team math competitions encouraging tauira māori and pacific to excel in mathematics. Events are run throughout term 2 and 3 and hosted by schools. You will work with school leaders, teachers, community groups, students and whānau to strengthen engagement, advance educational success and support successful transitions into university study. Your responsibilities will include: Support the strategic planning, delivery and ongoing development of pathway programmes. Build and maintain strong relationships with schools, community organisations, Māori and Pacific stakeholders, and internal University partners. Deliver presentations and engagement activities for students, families and educators. Support programme reporting, evaluation and continuous improvement activities. Assist with marketing, communications and outreach initiatives in partnership with University Marketing. Contribute to strategies that increase participation, achievement and successful tertiary transitions for priority learner groups. Coordinate with programme teams to ensure a high-quality participant experience and consistent programme delivery. He kōrero mōu | About you We're seeking someone who brings credibility within the education sector and is passionate about supporting student success. Candidates from the University’s 19 Partnership schools will be considered first, requiring principal sign-off. If there is no placement confirmed with partner schools within an (closing 1 December), the roles will then be offered externally. You will ideally have: A Bachelor's degree in Education. Teaching experience within a secondary school environment. Experience in a middle leadership, unit holder or similar educational leadership role. Strong stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills. Experience working collaboratively across diverse groups and communities. Excellent communication, presentation and organisational skills. Confidence using Microsoft Office and digital systems. The following will be highly regarded: A postgraduate qualification in Education. Experience leading initiatives focused on Māori and/or Pacific learner achievement. Experience analysing curriculum, achievement or NCEA data to inform planning and decision-making. Knowledge of secondary-to-tertiary pathways and the wider New Zealand education system. This position is classified as a Non-core Children's Worker under the Children's Act 2014. The successful candidate will be required to undergo and satisfy the University's safety checking requirements before commencing employment. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer At Waipapa Taumata Rau, you'll be part of an organisation dedicated to excellence, equity and creating positive impact across Aotearoa New Zealand. A tailored development plan, ensuring you return to your school community equipped with new skills, data capabilities, tertiary knowledge, and learner success insights, that can support wider school innovations, and ongoing career progression. The opportunity to influence educational outcomes for future generations. A collaborative and purpose-driven team environment. Access to staff benefits and professional development opportunities. A commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and Te Tiriti o Waitangi. There are two full-time, fixed term positions available: 12 month fixed term position 6 month fixed term position Remote working is not available for this position. As part of the placement programme, the university will partner with the school, paying $70,000/ 6 months, and $140,000/12 months directly to the school. The successful candidate will placed into the role as a cross-organisation secondment. If the roles go external to the partnerships, the salary range for this position is between $73,400 - $90,700 (Band F) depending on skills and experience. For more detailed information, please refer to the position description. Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to Apply If you're passionate about education, community engagement and supporting students to realise their potential, we'd love to hear from you. Apply now and help create pathways that empower learners to thrive at the University of Auckland and beyond. Applications should be submitted online, before the closing date of Sunday, 1 December 2026 and include an up-to-date CV and cover letter outlining what strengths you will bring to this role. Please note that we do not accept email applications. f you have any questions, please contact Katalina Ma via katalina.ma@auckland.ac.nz or Liletina Vaka via Liletina.vaka@auckland.ac.nz. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Content Creator Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Pathways Programmes Teacher Placement - Expression of Interest Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156670175": {
      "title": "University of Auckland IT Procurement Category Manager",
      "description": "University of Auckland IT Procurement Category Manager | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . IT Procurement Category Manager Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60022534 UoA Department Name: Strategic Procurement Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity This is an opportunity to play a key role in shaping the University’s approach to strategic IT procurement. Working within Procurement and OneFinance, you will lead end-to-end sourcing and category management activities, helping to deliver value for money, manage commercial risk, and support the University’s broader strategic objectives through effective supplier and stakeholder partnerships. Lead complex sourcing activities from planning and market engagement through to supplier selection, negotiation, contract execution, and ongoing supplier management. Develop and implement category strategies for IT-related spend, informed by market insights, stakeholder needs, risk assessments, and business priorities. Build trusted relationships with stakeholders across the University, providing expert procurement advice and supporting informed commercial decision-making. Manage strategic supplier relationships, driving performance, innovation, value creation, and continuous improvement throughout the contract lifecycle. Analyse spend, market trends, and supplier performance to identify opportunities for cost optimisation, service improvements, and risk mitigation. Champion best-practice procurement processes, ensuring compliance with University policies, regulatory requirements, and ethical procurement standards. Embed environmental, social and governance (ESG) considerations into procurement activities, supporting the University’s sustainability and strategic goals. This is a full-time (37.5 hours per week), 24-month Fixed Term position. The salary range is $118,000-$136,500pa plus benefits. For more detailed information, please refer to the Position Description. He kōrero mōu | About You You are an experienced procurement professional who combines commercial acumen with strong relationship management skills. Comfortable working in complex stakeholder environments, you bring a strategic mindset, strong analytical capability, and a collaborative approach that enables you to influence outcomes and deliver value across a broad range of procurement activities. Proven experience in procurement, category management, supplier relationship management, and contract management, ideally within a large and diverse organisation. Demonstrated ability to lead end-to-end sourcing projects, including tendering, evaluation, negotiation, and contract implementation. Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret spend data, assess market conditions, evaluate risks, and develop evidence-based procurement strategies. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the confidence to influence, advise, and build credibility at all levels of an organisation. Well-developed commercial and negotiation skills, with a track record of achieving positive outcomes and managing supplier performance. A customer-focused and collaborative approach, coupled with sound judgement, integrity, and a commitment to ethical procurement practices. Ability to manage competing priorities, adapt to changing business needs, and drive continuous improvement initiatives. A recognised tertiary qualification in procurement, supply chain management, business, or a related discipline. Experience within technology, digital, or IT procurement environments, together with an understanding of sustainable procurement and ESG principles, would be highly advantageous. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices (including working from home if feasible, flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online, by the closing date of Sunday 8th November, 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting how you can meet the skills and experiences detailed above. Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend Posted by Joshua Chapman share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Procure to Pay Administrator Auckland, New Zealand Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Research Operation Coordinator Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. IT Procurement Category Manager Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156668439": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Te Terenga",
      "description": "University of Auckland Te Terenga | Schools and Community Engagement Adviser | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Te Terenga | Schools and Community Engagement Adviser Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019816 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6,000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties and 13 service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. The University of Auckland creates globally transformative impacts through our distinctive strengths in world-leading research, scholarship, teaching, and collaborative partnerships, inspired by our unique position in Aotearoa New Zealand and the Asia-Pacific. Our mission and values place a strong emphasis on our student body and scholarly community, and we work with both the community and enterprise to advance the well-being of the people of Auckland and New Zealand, with a clear commitment to sustainability . Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity As our Te Terenga | Schools and Community Engagement Adviser , you will play a pivotal role in building meaningful, mana-enhancing relationships with secondary schools, students, and whānau. This role is grounded in guidance, partnership, and long-term relationship‑building that supports school leavers as they explore study pathways and navigate their transition to university. You will work across targeted secondary schools and community groups to deliver high-quality engagement activities, develop tailored outreach plans, and co-create pathways that help turn potential into possibility. Your work will ensure students and whānau have the information, support, and confidence they need to make informed decisions about their futures and move through the journey to application and enrolment. Ngā Haepapa Matua | Key Responsibilities (not limited to): Combine strategy, relationship‑building, and digital innovation to grow engagement and deliver a seamless, mana‑enhancing school‑leaver experience. Develop and nurture strong, mana‑enhancing partnerships with secondary schools, careers advisers, teachers, community groups, whānau and internal stakeholders. Deliver engaging presentations, workshops, events, and outreach activities that inspire and inform students and whānau. Develop and execute tailored engagement plans across your allocated school and community portfolio. Provide accurate, relevant advice to prospective students and support them throughout the school‑leaver journey. Champion the use of digital outreach tools and innovative engagement approaches to extend reach and enhance the quality of engagement. Identify new opportunities to strengthen engagement, grow awareness, and improve services offered to schools and communities. Contribute to continuous improvement across the Schools and Community Engagement team, ensuring activities uphold a positive, inclusive experience for all. He kōrero mōu | About you You are a confident communicator and relationship‑builder who enjoys working with young people, whānau and school communities. You bring warmth, energy and professionalism to presentations and conversations and thrive in a role that requires collaboration, adaptability and cultural competence. You will bring: A relevant degree or equivalent experience. Strong understanding of the New Zealand secondary school environment. Demonstrated competence and confidence in te ao Māori. Proven experience building and maintaining strong stakeholder relationships. Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to engage diverse audiences. Experience using digital engagement tools and delivering online outreach. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to work effectively during peak periods. A full, clean New Zealand driver's licence. Ability to obtain and maintain full Police Vetting clearance. Understanding of the tertiary environment and student experience is advantageous. The salary range is $73,400 to $90,700 per annum, Band F- depending on skills and experience. This is a full-time (37.5 hours per week) permanent position. For more detailed information, please refer to the Position Description He kōrero mōu | About you You are a confident communicator and strategic relationship-builder who thrives in a complex, people-focused environment. You bring: A degree (postgraduate qualification advantageous) or equivalent experience. Strong understanding of the NZ secondary school system. Proven experience building and maintaining stakeholder relationships. Demonstrated competence and confidence in te ao Māori. Excellent presentation and engagement skills. Experience delivering digital engagement tools and resources. The ability to work collaboratively, think strategically, and execute effectively. Full NZ drivers licence Ability to successfully obtain and maintain full Police Vetting clearance An understanding of the tertiary education environment and student experience is advantageous. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university and maintains significant computational, laboratory, and analytic facilities. Auckland itself is frequently ranked among the world’s most liveable cities. The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices (including working from home, flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of 10th October 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV, highlighting how you can meet the skills and experience detailed above. Please reach out to Liletina Vaka (Associate Director Schools and Community Engagement) via liletina.vaka@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. #LI-DNI Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Content Creator Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Te Terenga | Schools and Community Engagement Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156662813": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Te Ūnga Kairuruku, Schools and Community Recruitment Adviser",
      "description": "University of Auckland Te Ūnga Kairuruku, Schools and Community Recruitment Adviser | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Te Ūnga Kairuruku, Schools and Community Recruitment Adviser Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 55568062 UoA Department Name: Schools and Community Engagement Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university, with a turnover of $1.3bn, including research revenue of over $300m generated across eight diverse faculties and two research institutes. We employ more than 5400 academic and professional staff to support over 45,000 students, making us one of NZ’s largest employers. The University of Auckland creates globally transformative impacts through our distinctive strengths in world-leading research, scholarship, teaching, and collaborative partnerships, inspired by our unique position in Aotearoa New Zealand and the Asia-Pacific. Our mission and values place a strong emphasis on our student body and scholarly community, and we work with both the community and enterprise to advance the well-being of the people of Auckland and New Zealand, with a clear commitment to sustainability . Job Description The opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi Te Ūnga Kairuruku, Schools and Community Recruitment Adviser , will be a key team member to implement recruitment initiatives for the school leaver market. You will be responsible for delivering mana-enhancing and inspiring activities for Years 13 secondary school students and maintaining a strong pipeline of opportunities for students to engage with Waipapa Taumata Rau. You will recruit new students into the university, through targeted events and will work with designated faculties in their portfolio of programmes as a relationship manager, ensuring that Faculties needs are being communicated and met by the Schools and Community Engagement function. This is a great opportunity for an experienced student adviser to specialise in a portfolio of programmes and industries. Mō tō mātou rōpū | About the team Ko Waipapa Taumata Rau ko au, Ko au ko Waipapa Taumata Rau The pōwhiri; a traditional tikanga based welcome for all. Bringing people together to share, engage and form a bond as one. The University of Auckland encapsulates this process as an essential model to welcome new prospective students and their whānau to the University. The Schools and Community Engagement Office champion the values of Taumata Teitei, a Vision 2030 and a 2025 Strategic Plan for the University of Auckland.  Their engagements will be mana enhancing, their kōrero inspiring and their actions empowering in preparing secondary students for their journey and the next phases of their voyage through education. This is a full-time (37.5 hours per week), permanent position. The salary range is $73,400 to $90,700 per annum - Band F, depending on skills and experience. For more detailed information, please refer to the position description . Qualifications About you | He kōrero mōu Are you eager to take on an exciting opportunity? We are looking for a welcoming, motivated person with drive and desire to make a positive difference to the Schools and Community Engagement Team through a proven record of successful stakeholder engagement skills and an approach to work that embraces manakitanga, whanaungatanga, kaitiakitanga, flexibility and diversity. For a detailed description of the key tasks and responsibilities, please see the attached position description, however, to be successful in the role you will need to have the following attributes: A tertiary level qualification or equivalent experience Proven experience developing and maintaining relationships with key stakeholders. Experience of working with and understanding the needs of a diverse range of clients. Highly skilled communicator and presenter. Proficient computer literacy abilities and experience in delivering digital tools and resources. An understanding of the NZ secondary school system Have in-depth understanding of the tertiary environment especially in relation to the student experience. Demonstrable understanding, competence and confidence of te ao Māori Kia Whakamana i te Tangata - acknowledging, maintaining and restoring the mana and tapu of individuals, whānau and communities. Agile experience, or an understanding of cross-function team ways of working in an agile environment. Ability to work with complex data Flexibility to support after hour events and ability to travel independently. Additional Information Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices (including working from home, flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online, by the closing date of 01 November 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV highlighting how you can meet the skills and experiences detailed above. Please reach out to Papalii Michael ( p.m.mauu@auckland.ac.nz ) if you have any questions about the role. Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive and equitable environment. For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQITakatāpui+, people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other equity issues go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz . #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Content Creator Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Te Ūnga Kairuruku, Schools and Community Recruitment Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
