    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156430319": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Brand Adviser",
      "description": "University of Auckland Brand Adviser | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Brand Adviser Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 60019781 UoA Department Name: Marketing and Recruitment Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers.  We have six academic faculties, two large-scale research institutes and a number of professional service divisions creating a diverse, dynamic and complex organisational culture that demands excellence. Our lecturers and researchers are regarded as experts in their fields, frequently directing global research projects designed to better the lives of New Zealanders and the world, and in turn passing this knowledge on to our students. Job Description Te whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity Reporting to the Brand Manager within the Marketing and Recruitment function of the Strategic Engagement portfolio, you’ll provide specialist brand advice and coordinate the end-to-end delivery of brand activation and promotional initiatives across the University. This role offers an opportunity to play a key role in strengthening the University of Auckland’s brand and reputation while supporting the delivery of initiatives that engage audiences and contribute to University-wide priorities. Key areas of focus include: Coordinating and delivering brand activation, events and promotional initiatives, managing timelines, approvals. Providing practical brand advice to internal stakeholders and ensuring brand assets, marketing materials and communications are applied consistently. Coordinating brand content and collateral across Marketing, Content, Design and Social Media teams, including proofreading and quality assurance Supporting sponsorship and partnership activation, merchandise, supplier relationships and associated administrative and budget processes Building strong stakeholder relationships and identifying opportunities to improve brand processes, templates and ways of working. We have two full-time, permanent opportunities available . The full salary range for these roles are $73,400 - $99,400 per annum (Band F). For more detailed information about the role and requirements, please refer to the position description . He kōrero mōu | About you We’re looking for someone who brings strong organisational and coordination skills, excellent attention to detail and a practical understanding of brand and marketing delivery. You’ll be confident providing advice to a range of stakeholders and translating brand strategy and guidelines into practical recommendations and high-quality outputs. We’re particularly interested in people who bring: Experience delivering brand, marketing, events or promotional activity, ideally within a large or complex organisation Strong coordination, organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, timelines and deliverables Experience providing practical advice to stakeholders and applying brand strategy and guidelines to marketing activity Excellent attention to detail, proofreading and quality assurance skills, alongside strong written and verbal communication Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer This role offers the opportunity to contribute to the continued development and strengthening of the University of Auckland’s brand, working within a collaborative Marketing and Recruitment function that brings together specialist expertise across brand, marketing, student recruitment, market research, campaigns, events, partnerships and promotional activity. You’ll have the opportunity to build strong stakeholder relationships, contribute to University-wide initiatives and help improve the processes, tools and ways of working that support consistent and effective brand delivery. Additional Information Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of 29th of October 2026. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting your interest in the role, your capabilities and relevant experience. Reasonable accommodations - We are committed to building a more equitable and inclusive workforce and workplace, so we encourage applicants to reach out to discuss any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process, including alternative ways to submit applications. Whānau and support people - Should you be invited to an interview for this role, your whānau members and/or support people will be welcome to join you. The recruiter or hiring manager will provide more information about this as part of the interview arrangements. Please reach out to Laura McPike, Brand Manager - Laura.McPike@auckland.ac.nz for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. #LI-DNI Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Student Support Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Doctoral Candidate Advisor Auckland, New Zealand Marketing Content Creator Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Brand Adviser Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156408849": {
      "title": "University of Auckland Global Networks Manager",
      "description": "University of Auckland Global Networks Manager | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Global Networks Manager Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 55559311 UoA Department Name: Intl Global Partnerships & Development Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are seeking a Global Networks Manager to lead and strengthen the University’s engagement across key international networks, including Universitas 21 (U21), the Association of Pacific Rim Universities (APRU), and the Worldwide Universities Network (WUN). This role is instrumental in maximising the value of these strategic partnerships, supporting the University’s internationalisation objectives, research ambitions, education portfolio and global reputation. Working closely with senior leaders, faculties, service divisions and international partners, you will design and deliver engagement plans that translate strategic priorities into meaningful outcomes. You will provide advice, coordination and oversight across a diverse portfolio of partnership activities, ensuring opportunities arising from these networks are visible, accessible and aligned with University objectives. This is a highly relationship-focused role that combines strategic planning, stakeholder engagement and programme delivery. You will represent the University in international forums, support senior leaders involved in network governance, and help drive engagement across research, learning abroad, institutional partnerships and global collaboration initiatives. Domestic and international travel, along with occasional evening and weekend work, will be required. Your responsibilities will include: Leading the University’s engagement across U21, APRU and WUN, ensuring activity delivers measurable value and strategic impact Developing and delivering annual engagement plans, reporting frameworks and communication initiatives that support network participation Building strong relationships with senior leaders, faculties, service divisions and global partners to maximise partnership outcomes Identifying and promoting opportunities across research, teaching and learning, student mobility, internationalisation and institutional collaboration Supporting senior University representatives through briefings, governance support, reporting and strategic advice Driving continuous improvement through evaluation, benchmarking and the development of effective engagement processes and practices This is a permanent full-time position (37.5 hours per week). The salary range for this role is $98,000 to $105,000 , negotiable depending on skills and experience. A full description of your duties and the role are provided in the position description linked HERE . He kōrero mōu | About you You are an experienced relationship manager who enjoys working across complex stakeholder environments to deliver strategic outcomes. You bring a strong understanding of international partnerships and are confident engaging with senior leaders, academics, researchers and external organisations in a professional and culturally responsive manner. You are highly organised, able to balance multiple priorities, and comfortable working both strategically and operationally. You enjoy identifying opportunities, connecting people, and turning ideas into action. Your communication skills allow you to build trust and influence outcomes, and you are motivated by contributing to initiatives that strengthen the University's global profile and international partnerships. E rapua ana mātou | We are seeking A relevant tertiary qualification and significant experience within the tertiary education sector or a similarly complex environment Experience managing strategic partnerships, international networks or institutional relationships across multiple stakeholders Demonstrated ability to translate strategic priorities into operational plans and deliver measurable outcomes Strong stakeholder engagement, relationship management and influencing skills, including experience working with senior leaders Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including reporting, presentations and the preparation of strategic briefings Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities and deadlines in a complex environment Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university, guided by a commitment to excellence and service to our communities. With more than 6,000 academic and professional staff, we support a diverse community of over 47,000 students. Guided by our values , we work collaboratively to advance knowledge, foster equity and inclusion, and contribute meaningfully to New Zealand’s social, cultural, and economic well-being. We cultivate an environment that supports your growth and rewards excellence with a range of staff benefits , including: Competitive salary and five weeks of annual leave Discounted public Transport for permanent and long-term fixed term staff Superannuation/KiwiSaver , matching up to 6.75% Flexible working arrangements, including working from home and flexible hours Leading, and inclusive parental leave provisions Career development opportunities and a range of benefits, including discounted insurance , memberships , and on‑site amenities Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Please submit your application online by the closing date of Sunday, 1 November 2026 . Your application should include: A brief Cover Letter explaining why you're interested in this role and how your skills match the requirements. Your updated CV . Please note that we do not accept email applications. Applicants who are currently based in New Zealand and hold current New Zealand work rights will be prioritised. Overseas applicants will be considered; however, only those who can demonstrate direct experience in a comparable role are likely to progress through the shortlisting process. If you have specific questions that you cannot find the answers to in the advertisement or position description, you are welcome to contact Natasha Ager, Associate Director Global Partnerships and Development at natasha.ager@auckland.ac.n z Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at University of Auckland Business Development Manager – Postgraduate Māori and Pacific Auckland, New Zealand Lecturer in Dance Studies Auckland, New Zealand Professional Teaching Fellow Auckland, New Zealand Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. × Continue Global Networks Manager Auckland, New Zealand Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156224264": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer-Pharmacy-Prescribing & Advanced Scopes of Practice",
      "description": "University of Auckland Lecturer/Snr Lecturer-Pharmacy-Prescribing & Advanced Scopes of Practice | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer/Snr Lecturer-Pharmacy-Prescribing & Advanced Scopes of Practice Full-time Campus: Grafton Campus Position Number: 60022827 UoA Department Name: Pharmacy Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is Aotearoa New Zealand’s leading university. With more than 6,000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are proud to be one of the country’s largest and most diverse employers. Our people are driven by curiosity, purpose and a shared commitment to creating positive impact for our communities. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity Advance pharmacist prescribing and evolving scopes of pharmacy practice through contemporary education, scholarship and sector engagement. The School of Pharmacy is seeking a current or recent pharmacist prescriber with expertise in prescribing education, advanced clinical practice and workforce development. You will lead and shape education that supports safe, evidence-informed pharmacist prescribing and prepares pharmacists to practise effectively within evolving scopes and models of collaborative care. While this appointment has a particular initial focus in this area, the successful candidate will contribute more broadly to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, supervision and academic activities – particularly those with a focus on prescribing – across the School of Pharmacy according to their expertise and the evolving needs of the School. Key responsibilities Develop, deliver and evaluate postgraduate and undergraduate teaching relevant to prescribing and advanced pharmacy practice. Contribute to learning in clinical assessment, clinical reasoning, pharmacotherapeutics, prescribing, monitoring, and collaborative care. Develop authentic assessments of clinical and prescribing competence, including case-based, workplace-based and/or performance approaches. Build relationships with prescribers, health services, regulators, Māori and Pacific health providers, professional organisations and interprofessional partners. Support workplace supervisors and learners and contribute to curriculum currency, accreditation readiness and continuous improvement. Coordinate courses or modules and contribute to curriculum review and continuous improvement. Enhance student learning and engagement, responding constructively to student and peer review feedback Develop and implement innovations in teaching and assessment, and evaluate their impact through peer review Supervise undergraduate and postgraduate students, and develop research or scholarship in prescribing, medicines optimisation, advanced practice, implementation or workforce development. Lead and contribute to service activities within the School, Faculty, and wider University community This is a permanent, full-time position , though a part-time role may be considered depending on the successful candidate's needs. We are ideally seeking someone who can commence February 2027, however we can be flexible on the start date for the right person. The appointment may be made at Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level. Academic level and salary step will be determined by qualifications, experience and achievement against the University’s academic standards. The salary range for this role is $99,788 - $145,741 depending on skills and experience. For more detailed information, please review the position description for Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Pharmacy He kōrero mōu | About you You will be a pharmacist prescriber with at least 12 months' experience prescribing as a pharmacist prescriber, with a strong understanding of safe prescribing and collaborative care. We are particularly interested in candidates who hold a current pharmacist-prescriber registration, or are eligible to hold one, or bring equivalent expertise in advanced clinical practice. You will be collegial, adaptable and able to contribute beyond your principal area of expertise. You will bring a commitment to excellent student learning, evidence-informed educational practice, impactful research or scholarship, and equitable outcomes for Māori and other communities. Ngā Pūkenga Motuhake | Important skills A postgraduate clinical degree in pharmacy – ideally in prescribing – with associated clinical experience. Registration, or eligibility for registration, as a pharmacist prescriber in New Zealand. Experience teaching pharmacy, prescribing or other health-professional learners. Experience providing direct patient care in diverse pharmacy settings Expertise in one or more of prescribing, advanced clinical practice, patient assessment, clinical reasoning, medicines optimisation and interprofessional care. Excellent communication, interpersonal and collaborative working skills. Motivated and self-directed to learn and take on new challenges Effective organisation and time management skills Evidence of research or scholarship achievement and potential appropriate to Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level. For appointment as Senior Lecturer, evidence of leadership in postgraduate education, curriculum, research, clinical partnerships and/or postgraduate supervision. Demonstrated commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi, cultural safety and equitable access to advanced pharmacy services. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university and maintains significant clinical, laboratory and analytic facilities. Auckland itself is frequently rated as one of the world’s most liveable cities. The University of Auckland is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices and a culture that supports work-life balance Career development programmes A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave 6.75% superannuation scheme In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by Tuesday 3 November 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting how you meet the skills and experiences detailed above. For a confidential conversation, please contact the Head of School, Associate Professor Amy Chan ( [email protected] ) Postgraduate Clinical Pharmacy Specialisation Lead Dr Rhys Ponton ( [email protected] ) Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156201660": {
      "title": "Digital Library Specialist",
      "description": "University of Auckland Digital Library Specialist | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Digital Library Specialist Full-time Campus: Auckland City Campus Position Number: 55567574 UoA Department Name: Content Discovery and Innovation Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading University. With over 6000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are one of NZ’s largest employers. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity We are searching for a Digital Library Specialist to join the Content Discovery and Innovation (CDI) team within Library Services at Te Kahu Tauira | Student and Scholarly Services (SaSS). In this role, you will provide specialist skills to ensure that the library collections application software delivers a customer-focused experience. As part of the CDI team, you will be responsible for the administrative configuration and Tier 2/3 customer support of Library collections application software, assisting in the evaluation, testing and communication of new product features and improvements. You will participate in projects to review and redesign business processes related to the use of the library collections application software. Library collection application software include: Integrated library management system (Alma), Discovery layer (Primo), Reading list (Talis), Institutional repository (DSpace), Subject guides (LibGuides), Archives management systems (ArchiveSpace & Vernon), Interlibrary loan and Acquisition platforms, Access and authentication (OpenAthens). Salary Range: $87,000-$107,500 NZD per annum depending on experience and qualifications. This is a full-time, 37.5 hours per week role on a permanent contract. For more detailed information, please refer to the Position Description. He kōrero mōu | About you Degree and/or postgraduate qualification in information management, information science or equivalent, or the equivalent knowledge, skills and understanding gained through extensive work-related experience. You will operate with energy and passion, demonstrate a collaborative approach to work well with others, and model best practice principles and behaviours. Nga Pūkenga Motuhake | Important Skills 3 to 5 years' experience, preferably 2 to 3 years working with collection applications software. Experience in supporting and developing library application software. Experience in developing and implementing processes, systems and services. Experience creating, documenting, and implementing best practices and workflows. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand's leading University and maintains significant computational, laboratory, and analytic facilities. Auckland is frequently rated as one of the world's most liveable cities. The University is committed to providing an excellent working environment through the following: Flexible employment practices (including working from home and flexible hours) Up to 6.75% company superannuation scheme A competitive salary with five weeks' annual leave In addition, we also offer career development programs, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by the closing date of 3/11/26 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and CV highlighting how you can meet the abovementioned skills and experiences. Please note that we may close the advert earlier if we find a suitable candidate. Please reach out to Jo Simons - [email protected] for a confidential conversation. Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TheUniversityOfAuckland/744000156196849": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Auckland Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Pharmacy - Clinical and Professional Skills | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Pharmacy - Clinical and Professional Skills Full-time Campus: Grafton Campus Position Number: 60022825 UoA Department Name: Pharmacy Company Description Waipapa Taumata Rau | The University of Auckland The University of Auckland is Aotearoa New Zealand’s leading university. With more than 6,000 academic and professional staff supporting over 46,000 students, we are proud to be one of the country’s largest and most diverse employers. Our people are driven by curiosity, purpose and a shared commitment to creating positive impact for our communities. Job Description Te Whiwhinga mahi | The opportunity The School of Pharmacy is seeking a pharmacist educator with particular expertise in clinical and professional skills education in pharmacy. You will help shape integrated learning in areas such as patient consultation, communication, clinical reasoning, patient assessment, medicines optimisation and professional practice. You may also contribute to simulation, practical teaching and authentic assessment of learners’ readiness for practice. While this appointment has a particular initial focus in this area, the successful candidate may contribute more broadly to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, research, supervision and academic activities across the School of Pharmacy according to their expertise and the evolving needs of the School. Key responsibilities Develop, deliver and evaluate high-quality pharmacy teaching, as agreed with the Head of School and senior academic leadership Contribute to integrated curriculum design across consultation skills, clinical reasoning, patient assessment, communication, medicines optimisation and professional practice. Develop and quality-assure authentic assessments, which may include simulation, OSCEs, practical assessments and other performance-based approaches. Coordinate courses or modules and contribute to curriculum review and continuous improvement. Enhance student learning and engagement, responding constructively to student and peer review feedback Develop and implement innovations in teaching and assessment, and evaluate their impact through peer review Supervise undergraduate, and where appropriate, postgraduate research projects, as appropriate to academic level and experience. Develop a research or scholarship programme and contribute to service and engagement within the School, Faculty, profession and wider community, as appropriate to academic level and experience. Lead and contribute to service activities within the School, Faculty, and wider University community This is a permanent, full-time position , though a part-time role may be considered depending on the successful candidate's needs. We are ideally seeking someone who can commence February 2027, however we can be flexible on the start date for the right person. The appointment may be made at Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level. Academic level and salary step will be determined by qualifications, experience and achievement against the University’s academic standards. The salary range for this role is $99,788 - $145,741 depending on skills and experience. For more detailed information, please review the position description for Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Pharmacy He kōrero mōu | About you You will be a registered pharmacist with at least 12 months' experience working in community and /or primary care pharmacy practice and an enthusiasm for teaching students and developing future health professionals. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience in clinical skills education, simulation, OSCEs or other approaches to assessment. You will be collegial, adaptable and able to contribute beyond your principal area of expertise. You will bring a commitment to excellent student learning, evidence-informed educational practice, and equitable outcomes for Māori and other communities. Ngā Pūkenga Motuhake | Important skills Registration, or eligibility for registration, as a pharmacist in New Zealand. Experience teaching pharmacy or other health-professional learners. Experience providing direct patient care in a community and /or primary care pharmacy setting Expertise in one or more of clinical reasoning, patient assessment, consultation and communication, medicines optimisation, simulation or performance-based assessment. Excellent communication, interpersonal and collaborative working skills. Motivated and self-directed to learn and take on new challenges Effective organisation and time management skills For appointment as Senior Lecturer, evidence of academic leadership in teaching, curriculum, assessment, research and/or postgraduate supervision. Demonstrated commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi, cultural safety and equitable health and education outcomes. Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou | What we offer The University of Auckland is New Zealand’s leading university and maintains significant clinical, laboratory and analytic facilities. Auckland itself is frequently rated as one of the world’s most liveable cities. The University of Auckland is committed to providing an excellent working environment through: Flexible employment practices and a culture that supports work-life balance Career development programmes A competitive salary with five weeks’ annual leave 6.75% superannuation scheme In addition, we also offer career development programmes, discounted car parking, a generous parental leave allowance, childcare, and a number of other discounts on internal and external services. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits. For more information, please visit Staff Benefits . Me pēhea te tuku tono | How to apply Applications must be submitted online by Tuesday 3 November 2026 to be considered. Please include your cover letter and your CV highlighting how you meet the skills and experiences detailed above. For a confidential conversation, please contact the Head of School, Associate Professor Amy Chan ( [email protected] ). Please note we are happy to answer your questions, but we do not accept applications by email. Additional Information Equity The University is committed to meeting its obligations under the Treaty of Waitangi and achieving equity outcomes for staff and students in a safe, inclusive, and equitable environment.  For further information on services for Māori, Pacific, women, LGBTQIATakatāpu iMVPFAFF + , people with disabilities, parenting support, flexible work and other personal circumstances go to www.equity.auckland.ac.nz By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
